  "label": "Harmful",
  "description": "The meme humorously mocks the concept of intelligence by juxtaposing a low IQ score (80) with the idea of being the 'highest in your village,' implying that intelligence is relative and context-dependent. This relies on the real-world stereotype that intelligence is often mocked or undervalued when it is not recognized as exceptional in a specific social or cultural context. The meme uses this stereotype to create humor by highlighting the absurdity of such a situation. While not explicitly targeting any specific group, it may unintentionally reinforce ableist stereotypes by making light of intellectual achievement, which can be perceived as dismissive or demeaning in certain contexts.",
